Fedora @RELEASE@ Live for Microsoft Surface Pro 11 (Snapdragon X Elite, OLED, incl. 5G SKU)

Kernel:        @ABI@ (ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11 @COMMIT@, mode: @MODE@); the stock Fedora kernel is removed.
Device tree:   @DTB@ (loaded explicitly by GRUB; installed system uses GRUB_DEVICETREE in BLS entries)
Built:         @DATE@ for SKU @SKU@
Base media:    @MEDIA@
Edition:       @EDITION_NOTE@
Secure Boot:   must be DISABLED (unsigned kernel).

Live session:  Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, GPU acceleration, touch and pen work. Audio and battery status are
               unavailable on the live USB because the audio DSP is kept off while booting from USB-C
               (modprobe.blacklist=qcom_q6v5_pas). They work after installation to the internal disk.

Installation:  run "Install to Hard Drive". The installed system boots this kernel with the Denali DTB;
               a one-shot service (sp11-first-boot) removes the live-only DSP blacklist on the first boot.
Sensors:       hexagonrpcd, libssc and iio-sensor-proxy with its Qualcomm Sensor Core drivers, plus this unit's
               sensor registry (sp11-sensors), are installed. They stay inactive on the live USB (the DSP is off)
               and serve the accelerometer, light sensor and compass on the installed system.

RPMs used to build this media are under /sp11/rpms.

Redistribution: this media and the RPMs under /sp11/rpms contain proprietary Qualcomm firmware and the
               sensor configuration and registry copied from the Windows installation of the machine that
               built it. Do not pass them on; build your own from the source repository instead.
Credits:       kernel ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11 (GPL-2.0); audio topology, UCM and pen integration
               from ooaklee/linux-surface-pro-11-oe; iptsd from linux-surface/iptsd; sensors from
               linux-msm/hexagonrpc (this project's fork), DylanVanAssche/libssc and Fedora's
               iio-sensor-proxy; Fedora @EDITION@ Live.
